<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Document</title>
</head>
<style>
.parent {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
}

.box9999 {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 9999;
    width: 200px;
    height: 200px;
    background: red;
}

/*
WHY IS 9999 BEHIND 1?

.box9999 has z-index: 9999, BUT it is trapped inside
the stacking context created by .parent.

The entire .parent stacking context has z-index: 1.
Therefore, .box9999 cannot escape its parent's stacking
context and jump above .box1, even though its own z-index
is 9999.

.box1 belongs to a higher stacking level than the
.parent stacking context, so it appears in front.
*/

.box1 {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 2;
    width: 200px;
    height: 200px;
    background: blue;
    top: 50px;
    left: 50px;
}
</style>
<body>
    <div class="parent">
    <div class="box9999">z-index: 9999</div>
</div>

<div class="box1">z-index: 1</div>
</body>
</html>
